---
import Screenshot from './Screenshot.astro';
import openBox from '../assets/screens/claude-code.png';

// The third pillar. Autonomy and safety are what make a discobox possible; this
// is what makes it something you would actually use every day.

const buckets = [
  {
    name: 'ssh, or a shell in one keystroke',
    body:
      'ssh $DISCOBOX_ID works the moment you run discobox admin ssh-config --write, and discobox shell drops you straight into the box. It is a host you can reach, not a session you have to negotiate with.',
    line: '$ ssh purple-mongoose',
  },
  {
    name: 'Your editor, attached',
    body:
      'Because it is a real ssh host, VS Code, Cursor, JetBrains and anything else with a remote mode open the box directly — discobox tools vscode launches yours at the right folder. You read and edit what the agent is working on in the editor you already use.',
    line: '$ discobox tools vscode',
  },
  {
    name: 'The desktop in your browser',
    body:
      'The box runs a desktop with a real browser on it, served over VNC and noVNC. Forward the port and you can watch the agent click through the app it just built, take the mouse when it gets stuck, or open the page yourself.',
    line: '$ discobox proxy --port 6080',
  },
  {
    name: 'git in, commits out',
    body:
      'Your source is cloned in and every box has its own git remote. Commits are cherry-picked onto your working tree when you apply, so you review history in the tools you already use — not a diff you have to trust.',
    line: '$ discobox apply purple-mongoose',
  },
  {
    name: 'Your toolchain comes along',
    body:
      'direnv is wired up, so nix, mise, or whatever your project already declares pulls your toolchain into the box on entry. Nothing to re-describe in a Dockerfile, and boxes launch in seconds with the agent ready to go.',
    line: 'direnv: loading .envrc · nix develop',
  },
  {
    name: 'Drive it or script it',
    body:
      'A TUI when you want to watch, a full OpenAPI surface and a scriptable CLI when you do not. Anything the interface does a shell script can do: create boxes, grant secrets, collect the results.',
    line: '$ discobox ls --output json',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="experience">
  <div class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experience</p>
    <h2 class="couplet__hook">The box is somewhere else. It should never feel like it.</h2>
    <p class="couplet__turn">
      The reason you work on your laptop is that everything is already there. A remote
      machine gives that up, and most sandboxes stop caring at that point. Most of
      Discobox is spent giving it back: ssh, a shell, your editor, the desktop over
      VNC, git — every one of them a command away. And it is the same architecture
      doing it, because every crossing already goes through a channel Discobox
      controls, which can just as well make the box feel local on the way in.
    </p>

    <Screenshot
      src={openBox}
      alt="One discobox open in the launcher: Claude Code working on the left, a shell on the right listing nested Docker containers, systemd services and listening sockets, with a forwarded port in the header."
      sizes="(min-width: 70.5rem) 68rem, calc(100vw - 2.5rem)"
      caption="One box, open: the agent on the left, a shell beside it, the services the repository declares as tabs, and a forwarded port in the header. Every key goes to the box."
    />

    <div class="buckets">
      {
        buckets.map((bucket) => (
          <div class="card bucket">
            <h3 class="bucket__name">{bucket.name}</h3>
            <p class="bucket__body">{bucket.body}</p>
            <p class="bucket__line">{bucket.line}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .buckets {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .buckets {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .bucket {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .bucket__name {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .bucket__body {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .bucket__line {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--magenta);
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
  }
</style>
